    "result_text": "Only draft claims can be edited now, and a voided claim keeps its number. `bin/e2e` passes all 4 tests in the spec.\n\n**Server** (`ClaimService.java`)\n- Editing a claim that isn't a draft is refused with 409 \"Only a draft claim can be edited.\" Nothing is written to the store or the audit file. This also blocks edits to settled and void claims, since the request says only a draft can be edited.\n- Voiding no longer clears the claim number, so the `CLAIM_VOIDED` record now ends with `number=N`. Voiding a draft still gives a line with no number. A number is never reused, because new numbers still come from the sheet's counter, which only goes up.\n- I updated the comment on `Claim.number` to say the number is kept after voiding.\n\n**Front end** (`claims.ts`)\n- Pressing Edit on a claim that isn't a draft shows `claim-error` on that claim's row (\"Only a draft claim can be edited. To change it, void it and add a new one.\") and doesn't open the editor.\n- If the server refuses an edit anyway, for example because another user opened the claim in the meantime, the form shows the same message in `claim-form-error`.\n\n**Stored data**\n- No schema change was needed. I added `V16__void_keeps_number.sql`, which only records the new rules and changes no data. Claims voided before this change have already lost their numbers, and those can't be restored.",
